course: dictionary
lesson: 14784
title: A word from church
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one place, like church. You may not meet psalter very often, but the words around it give clues. «The choir opened their psalters and began to sing.» Choirs sing, and they open something to sing from, so a psalter must be a book.
explain: «The old psalter had its letters painted by hand, in gold and red.» Old and painted by hand tell you it is a special book, made with care. Check your meaning by swapping it in: a book of the Psalms, used in church, still makes sense in each sentence.
explain: Psalter comes from church and the Bible. A clue like «the parish psalter» tells you it belongs to a church in a village or town. When the clues are not enough, a dictionary or a teacher can settle it.
fact: A psalter is a book containing the Psalms from the Bible.
fact: The Psalms are songs and prayers from the Bible.
fact: A psalter is used for worship in church.
fact: Some psalters are set out to be sung or said in church services.
fact: «A medieval psalter» means a psalter made long ago, in the Middle Ages.
exercise: «The choir opened their psalters and began to sing.» What is a psalter? | A kind of cake | *A book of Psalms from the Bible, used in church | A tin of paint | A pet bird
exercise: «The vicar read from the parish psalter during the service.» What is a parish psalter most likely used for? | Measuring the rain | Playing football | Cooking dinner | *Singing and reading in church services
exercise: Find and copy the word in «a medieval psalter» that tells you when it was made. | a | book | *medieval | psalter
test: «The monks painted every letter of the psalter by hand.» What does this sentence tell you about a psalter? | It was thrown away at once | *It was made carefully, by hand | It was a kind of food | It was printed by a machine in a shop
test: Which of these is a psalter? | A bag for shopping | A pet bird | *A book of Psalms used in church services | A kind of cake
exam: In a museum, a visitor reads about a medieval psalter. What does psalter mean? | *A book containing the Psalms from the Bible | A dish for baking | A map of the sea | A pen for writing letters
